---
import PageIntro from "@/components/PageIntro.astro";
import SiteFooter from "@/components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SubscribePanel from "@/components/SubscribePanel.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About us"
  description="Short reviews. No ads, sponsors, or PR leash. We love games and hold the people selling them accountable."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="content">
    <div class="reading">
      <PageIntro
        title={`About ${siteConfig.name}`}
        description="We love games. We're tired of the bullshit surrounding them."
      />
    </div>

    <section class="reading section--tight" aria-label="What we stand for">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why we're here</h2>
        <p>Gaming journalism has repeatedly let us down. Our take? Too many outlets seem more worried about losing access, early keys, and industry perks than telling readers a game is shit. We don't give a fuck about staying on a publisher's good side.</p>

        <h2>No ads. No sponsors. No leash.</h2>
        <p>Our opinions will never be bought with money, preview keys, or special treatment. Nobody gets a softer verdict because keeping them happy might benefit us.</p>

        <h2>Short reviews. Get on with your day.</h2>
        <p>What works, what sucks, and why. We don't need to hold you hostage for ten minutes to squeeze out another ad impression. Read it. Agree or disagree. Go play.</p>

        <h2>Games, not personal drama</h2>
        <p>We play every major release, plus smaller indie games that make a big splash. Someone's personal drama only matters here if it affects the actual game. Their Twitter argument isn't our fucking beat.</p>

        <h2>Nobody gets a pass</h2>
        <p>Favourite studios included. Make a stupid decision and we'll call it stupid. Act like fucking idiots and expect to hear about it. We don't pull punches, and we aren't pretending every game deserves praise.</p>

        <h2>Delay it. Finish it. Then sell it.</h2>
        <p>“The publisher made us ship” doesn't fix the game we paid for. We expect developers to push back, and publishers to give them the time. A delay earns more respect than unfinished garbage. Blame-shifting earns nothing.</p>
        <p>One game, one issue, updated as things change. Fix your mess and we'll acknowledge it. The launch doesn't disappear from the record.</p>

        <p>"A delayed game is eventually <strong>good</strong>, but a rushed game is forever <strong>bad</strong>"</p>

        <h2>Our points. Our judgment.</h2>
        <p>We made up our own scoring system. Developers start at 1,000; each game's score moves that total. Delivery, gameplay, writing, and value all count. It's opinion backed by reasons, not science. <a href="/scoring/">Read the scoring rules.</a></p>

        <h2>The team? Anonymous.</h2>
        <p>Judge the article, not the name above it. We're not building writer fan clubs or giving you a reason to dismiss a review because the same person disliked your favourite game. Disagree with the argument. Skip the crybaby grudge.</p>
        <p>Anonymous doesn't mean above correction. If we got something wrong, bring the receipts.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="reading section--tight">
      <p class="t-body t-dim">
        Corrections or questions? <a class="link" href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="container section">
      <SubscribePanel id="about-subscribe" />
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
